Hard cap on the bytes MLX allocates itself. Imported (no-copy) buffers count in
MLX's active memory but belong to the caller, so the allocator tracks them apart
(external) and a transient limit (0 = off) bounds active - external + cache:
a new buffer past it trims the cache, then throws a runtime_error tagged
[mlx-transient-cap]. get/reset expose the transient high-water.

